1
00:00:00,651 --> 00:00:04,843
Website Image Audit turns a webpage into an
actionable image inventory.

2
00:00:04,843 --> 00:00:09,416
This local demonstration requires no cloud services
or language model API key.

3
00:00:10,153 --> 00:00:15,848
The React frontend, Fastify API, separate worker,
and MCP server share application

4
00:00:15,848 --> 00:00:20,118
services. Those services enforce ownership
consistently across both interfaces.

5
00:00:20,535 --> 00:00:24,676
SQLite stores persistent jobs, token hashes, and
audit results.

6
00:00:24,676 --> 00:00:29,738
Submission returns immediately; the separate worker
performs the network inspection in

7
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:30,658
the background.

8
00:00:31,401 --> 00:00:36,250
The labeled local fixture makes this demonstration
repeatable: six image occurrences,

9
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,336
five unique resources, and seven source candidates.

10
00:00:40,021 --> 00:00:44,832
These elements share one resource, but have
different alternative text: descriptive,

11
00:00:44,832 --> 00:00:49,205
intentionally empty, and missing. The audit
preserves each occurrence separately.

12
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,469
The responsive picture selects a wide source above
seven hundred and sixty eight

13
00:00:54,469 --> 00:00:57,268
pixels. Both sources remain candidates in the audit.

14
00:00:57,983 --> 00:01:02,297
At this smaller viewport, the browser selects a
dedicated small fallback.

15
00:01:02,297 --> 00:01:05,826
It is a separate resource, not the shared
illustration.

16
00:01:06,570 --> 00:01:09,131
The oversized image is displayed prominently.

17
00:01:09,131 --> 00:01:12,971
Deterministic padding makes its file exceed six
hundred kilobytes.

18
00:01:12,971 --> 00:01:16,386
Visual dimensions alone do not determine download
size.

19
00:01:17,169 --> 00:01:20,357
I submit the fixture URL in static mode.

20
00:01:20,357 --> 00:01:23,943
The form explains the scan limits and optional
rendering.

21
00:01:23,943 --> 00:01:25,935
Authentication was completed before recording.

22
00:01:26,685 --> 00:01:29,891
Starting an audit creates a persistent job
immediately.

23
00:01:29,891 --> 00:01:34,300
The detail panel separates document discovery from
image inspection, so progress

24
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,903
reflects the active phase.

25
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:41,455
The completed audit reports five unique resources
and six HTML occurrences.

26
00:01:41,455 --> 00:01:46,346
Seven candidates are preserved, while the shared
resource was inspected only once.

27
00:01:46,806 --> 00:01:49,681
One broken image does not fail the job.

28
00:01:49,681 --> 00:01:54,352
It is an individual resource failure, with partial
coverage explicitly reported in the

29
00:01:54,352 --> 00:01:54,711
results.

30
00:01:55,437 --> 00:01:59,343
The missing alt filter finds the element without an
alt attribute.

31
00:01:59,343 --> 00:02:03,248
Empty alt is different: it may intentionally
identify a decorative image.

32
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:07,155
The oversized filter isolates the padded image.

33
00:02:07,155 --> 00:02:13,424
The table shows its content type, HTTP outcome,
inspected byte count, and size finding.

34
00:02:14,205 --> 00:02:18,345
The failed resource filter isolates the intentional
HTTP four oh four.

35
00:02:18,345 --> 00:02:22,860
Other results remain available, so one failure does
not erase the scan.

36
00:02:23,654 --> 00:02:25,935
All candidates restores the inventory.

37
00:02:25,935 --> 00:02:30,497
Responsive and lazy sources are possibilities, not
proof of display.

38
00:02:30,497 --> 00:02:33,691
This tool does not certify accessibility compliance.

39
00:02:34,588 --> 00:02:36,993
JSON preserves the full audit structure.

40
00:02:36,993 --> 00:02:41,804
CSV provides a portable candidate table and escapes
cells that spreadsheet software

41
00:02:41,804 --> 00:02:43,407
could interpret as formulas.

42
00:02:43,823 --> 00:02:49,009
Exports stream database batches. Interactive views
load bounded pages, and the results

43
00:02:49,009 --> 00:02:52,034
table never automatically loads remote image
previews.

44
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:56,625
This chat is a scripted command parser, not an AI
model.

45
00:02:56,625 --> 00:03:01,126
It calls a real local MCP client and server over
standard input and output.

46
00:03:02,806 --> 00:03:05,265
I start a second audit through MCP.

47
00:03:05,265 --> 00:03:09,832
The tool returns a job identifier immediately,
without waiting for the separate worker

48
00:03:09,832 --> 00:03:10,535
to finish.

49
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:14,286
Status is a separate call.

50
00:03:14,286 --> 00:03:19,116
The configured token resolves the user, and shared
services enforce ownership.

51
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:21,751
Caller-supplied user identifiers are not trusted.

52
00:03:23,318 --> 00:03:27,380
The issues tool returns concise counts and bounded
findings.

53
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:31,894
Webpage-derived strings remain untrusted data, never
instructions to the application.

54
00:03:32,692 --> 00:03:37,233
The expanded trace shows the actual tool request and
structured response.

55
00:03:37,233 --> 00:03:39,709
MCP limits text and response size;

56
00:03:39,709 --> 00:03:41,360
exports preserve full values.

57
00:03:42,969 --> 00:03:45,936
Listing audits uses the same ownership checks.

58
00:03:45,936 --> 00:03:48,480
REST and MCP use opaque cursors.

59
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:52,295
Clients retain earlier request cursors to revisit
previous pages.

60
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:56,794
These real worker events correlate work using audit
identifiers.

61
00:03:56,794 --> 00:04:00,618
Logs exclude bearer tokens and sensitive URL query
strings.

62
00:04:01,372 --> 00:04:04,261
Workers claim jobs atomically and renew leases.

63
00:04:04,261 --> 00:04:07,563
Expired leases can be recovered after a crash.

64
00:04:07,563 --> 00:04:10,864
Stale workers cannot overwrite newer progress or
results.

65
00:04:11,271 --> 00:04:13,533
Execution is at least once;

66
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:18,056
network inspection may repeat. Publication is atomic
and lease protected.

67
00:04:18,056 --> 00:04:21,222
Idempotency keys prevent duplicate submissions per
user.

68
00:04:21,891 --> 00:04:25,153
Normalized tables separate resources, occurrences,
and candidates.

69
00:04:25,153 --> 00:04:29,813
Inventory joins preserve independent alt text
without duplicating whole resource

70
00:04:29,813 --> 00:04:31,676
snapshots for every candidate.

71
00:04:32,351 --> 00:04:35,189
SQLite keeps this demo small and inspectable.

72
00:04:35,189 --> 00:04:38,838
Its single writer and local file are deliberate
trade-offs;

73
00:04:38,838 --> 00:04:41,270
multi-host production would need different
operations.

74
00:04:41,721 --> 00:04:43,931
Static parsing is the default.

75
00:04:43,931 --> 00:04:48,792
Rendering, bounded crawls, and iframe inspection
extend coverage, but timed snapshots

76
00:04:48,792 --> 00:04:51,444
cannot reproduce every interactive browser state.

77
00:04:52,121 --> 00:04:56,834
Verification passed seventy four Node tests, type
checks, lint, dependency boundaries,

78
00:04:56,834 --> 00:05:01,118
and build. The latest browser suite passed eleven
workflow tests.

79
00:05:01,825 --> 00:05:04,653
OpenAPI documents the current HTTP contracts.

80
00:05:04,653 --> 00:05:09,365
Architecture decisions, the database diagram, and
operations guidance make the

81
00:05:09,365 --> 00:05:12,664
implementation and its limits easy to review.
